Package: RieszCML
Type: Package
Title: Riesz Representer Based Targeted and One-Step Estimation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Christian", "Testa", email = "ctesta@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Salvador", "Balkus", email = "sbalkus@g.harvard.edu",
           role = "aut"),
    person("Nima", "Hejazi", email = "nhejazi@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "ths"))
  )
Description: Constructs asymptotically efficient one-step estimators and
    targeted minimum loss-based estimators (TMLEs) for statistical parameters
    that are linear functionals of one or more nuisance functions, or smooth
    transformations of such functionals. Each functional is specified through
    its nuisance estimates, Riesz representer, and efficient influence
    function using the 'RieszCurve' class; nested functionals, such as
    longitudinal treatment regimes, controlled direct effects, and estimands
    under outcome missingness or two-phase sampling, are built by chaining
    stages with the 'ComposedRieszCurve' class. Nuisance estimation is left to
    the user, so any regression procedure, including cross-fitted super
    learners, may be supplied. Delta-method helpers provide inference for
    contrasts, ratios, and odds ratios of fitted functionals.
